    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="1328" n="1316" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-08">8 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1071. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Acheson</hi>: Reference my 1053<anchor
                        n="77" xml:id="d646-f1"/> and your 93593,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d646-f2"/>
                    Chinese Govt, through Chief of Protocol has officially advised me that
                    appointment is favorably considered. Therefore please proceed without delay.</p>
                <pb facs="1329" n="1317" xml:id="pg1317"/>
                <p>I stated that I had not yet approached the President in the matter as I wished to
                    avoid the possibility of embarrassing him and Generalissimo in case latter was
                    not favorably impressed. I therefore requested Chinese to delay confidential
                    notification to their Ambassador until Presidential action was assured. I told
                    Protocol Chief that you would confidentially notify Chinese Ambassador before
                    nomination is made public. Also, at same time, please explain matters to General
                    Wedemeyer showing him 1058, and notify me.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
